00:12:07.917 --> 00:12:10.542
I'm liking all the rich colors on this mountain!

00:12:10.542 --> 00:12:13.042
I heard the Reaper did you in.

00:12:13.042 --> 00:12:15.583
It was touch-and-go there for a while.

00:12:15.583 --> 00:12:17.958
I'm young enough to recover quickly.

00:12:17.958 --> 00:12:20.125
Never mind that--hide your gun!

00:12:20.125 --> 00:12:22.750
Who's that? He has a gun!

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.208
M-Maybe we should call the police...

00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:28.167
Whoa! Whoa! N-No--that guy is, uh...

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:31.417
"Mr. Yoshioka from the local hunt club"
M-Mr. Yoshioka from the local hunt club.

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:34.375
Mr. Yoshioka?! But he's totally a foreigner!

00:12:34.375 --> 00:12:34.542
"He's an anime fan"
Mr. Yoshioka?! But he's totally a foreigner!

00:12:34.542 --> 00:12:38.417
"He's an anime fan"
H-He's naturalized. A big anime fan--you know.

00:12:38.417 --> 00:12:41.417
"He's an anime fan"
Oh, really?

00:12:41.417 --> 00:12:44.792
"He's an anime fan"
Well, enough about Mr. Yoshioka...

00:12:44.792 --> 00:12:50.083
Nagisa... be honest;
what do you think of me--

00:12:50.083 --> 00:12:52.958
--eeeYOW!

00:12:53.458 --> 00:12:54.250
Lovro...

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.625
The octopus invited me.

00:12:56.625 --> 00:13:00.250
I see. I'm just glad you're still alive, too.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.917
Your pupil's been worried. Go see her.

00:13:02.917 --> 00:13:03.750
I will.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:08.458
Wh-What's with the scary old dude?
He's no ordinary guy...

00:13:08.458 --> 00:13:13.333
M-Mild Yagyu. A big name
in the Asakusa theater scene.

00:13:13.333 --> 00:13:14.792
He's a comedian?!

00:13:14.792 --> 00:13:18.417
Th-That conversation?
They were discussing a bit.

00:13:18.417 --> 00:13:22.500
His pupil quit comedy, see,
and became a teacher here, and...

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.542
Hmm...

00:13:24.542 --> 00:13:28.958
What a tasty gun! You wouldn't think
kids put together this flavor!

00:13:28.958 --> 00:13:33.042
Yeah--it tastes so good,
I'd gladly eat even a poisoned bowl!

00:13:33.042 --> 00:13:35.458
F-Fellow comedians! From Asakusa!

00:13:35.458 --> 00:13:36.667
--And the guy eating the wasabi

00:13:36.667 --> 00:13:38.042
--Hm! Hm!
--And the guy eating the wasabi Mont Blanc

00:13:38.042 --> 00:13:39.917
is doing a reaction schtick he learned directly from Mild Yagyu!

00:13:39.917 --> 00:13:43.792
We just seem to fall in
with that kind of crowd.

00:13:43.792 --> 00:13:46.625
Hey, Nagisa...

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:48.708
You're lying, aren't you?

00:13:49.542 --> 00:13:52.458
My old man's a big-name talent.

00:13:52.458 --> 00:13:54.708
Since I was little, I've seen
the faces of tons of people

00:13:54.708 --> 00:13:57.083
who've cozied up to him.

00:13:57.833 --> 00:14:03.125
I can tell when people
put up a front, wear a fake smile.

00:14:03.125 --> 00:14:05.417
The girl I met at that island hotel?

00:14:05.417 --> 00:14:08.708
<i>She </i>wouldn't smile like that.

00:14:10.875 --> 00:14:13.042
Wow. Good eye.

00:14:13.042 --> 00:14:14.958
Nothing good about it.

00:14:14.958 --> 00:14:18.833
Just an unwanted talent
I got from my skeevy environment.

00:14:20.417 --> 00:14:23.667
You're right. I was lying to you.

00:14:23.667 --> 00:14:28.167
I've looked like this since I was
a little boy--I can't help it.

00:14:28.167 --> 00:14:29.417
And I always hated it.

00:14:29.417 --> 00:14:31.417
Wait--"boy"?

00:14:31.417 --> 00:14:33.958
But lately I've learned that

00:14:33.958 --> 00:14:38.250
if it can help others, even an
unwanted talent can give you confidence.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.667
So I don't hate it that much now.

00:14:41.667 --> 00:14:45.500
I'm sorry. I'm a guy.

00:14:47.292 --> 00:14:48.667
Another lie?

00:14:48.667 --> 00:14:49.500
No, really.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.542
<i>Another </i>one?

00:14:51.542 --> 00:14:52.542
No, <i>really</i>.

00:14:52.542 --> 00:14:52.667
Show him and he'll believe you!

00:14:52.667 --> 00:14:54.167
"Show him and he'll believe you!!"
Show him and he'll believe you!

00:14:54.167 --> 00:14:55.250
"Show him and he'll believe you!!"
Show him <i>what</i>?!

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.500
Show him <i>what</i>?!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.458
Does this look like a lying face?

00:14:59.458 --> 00:15:01.708
No way...

00:15:01.708 --> 00:15:03.417
Examined from another angle,

00:15:03.417 --> 00:15:06.000
your faults and weaknesses can be weapons.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:06.458
What I've learned in this classroom is how to do just that.

00:15:06.458 --> 00:15:09.375
"Sugar"
What I've learned in this classroom is how to do just that.

00:15:09.375 --> 00:15:13.417
"Sugar"
It's how we put together this café,

00:15:13.417 --> 00:15:18.833
and it's the connection that
brought all these people here today.

00:15:18.833 --> 00:15:22.625
It's really exciting--and fun.

00:15:26.417 --> 00:15:30.250
Oh, b-but since I tricked you,
I'll give you your money back!

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:35.583
Nah. I just... I feel like such a dummy.

00:15:35.583 --> 00:15:37.292
I'm out.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.833
Huh? He left already?

00:15:41.833 --> 00:15:42.292
"Heart-Pounding Maid Costume"
Huh? He left already?

00:15:42.292 --> 00:15:45.083
"Heart-Pounding Maid Costume"
I was going to soak him for a cosplay photo shoot.

00:15:45.083 --> 00:15:48.000
"Heart-Pounding Maid Costume"
Just how much were you trying to make off me?!

00:15:49.917 --> 00:15:54.000
Yuji... That was wrong of me.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.667
Well, our first day went all right...

00:16:01.667 --> 00:16:04.292
The sales reports've been posted.

00:16:04.292 --> 00:16:07.917
At this rate, we won't
get anywhere near the A Class.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.917
Hurry, or we'll miss the morning broadcast!

00:16:12.917 --> 00:16:14.542
Huh? A TV crew?

00:16:14.542 --> 00:16:16.000
Covering what?

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.458
The only thing up ahead is the E Class.

00:16:18.458 --> 00:16:19.125
"Smoked Freshwater Fish" "Acorn Café" "Persimmon-Loquat Gelatin"

00:16:19.125 --> 00:16:20.750
"Smoked Freshwater Fish" "Acorn Café" "Persimmon-Loquat Gelatin"
What the hell?!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.833
You guys! This online review
is spreading like wildfire!

00:16:24.833 --> 00:16:28.708
I dug around a little to find the source.

00:16:28.708 --> 00:16:30.417
And what I found...

00:16:30.417 --> 00:16:31.000
"Yuji Norita's Diary of a Wandering Gourmet"
And what I found...

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:35.375
"Yuji Norita's Diary of a Wandering Gourmet"
...was Yuji Norita--the most influential food blogger today!

00:16:35.375 --> 00:16:35.458
"Yuji Norita" "Curious about a place? I'll fly right over!"
...was Yuji Norita--the most influential food blogger today!

00:16:35.458 --> 00:16:38.583
"Yuji Norita" "Curious about a place? I'll fly right over!"
Thanks to having grown up eating lots of good food,

00:16:38.583 --> 00:16:41.833
"Yuji Norita" "Curious about a place? I'll fly right over!"
his tastebuds are, annoyingly enough, the real deal.

00:16:41.833 --> 00:16:46.417
His money-is-no-object wandering-gourmet
reviews are super reliable!

00:16:46.417 --> 00:16:48.208
Yuji...

00:16:49.542 --> 00:16:54.958
I came across a crazy-delicious café
at the Kunugigaoka School Festival.

00:16:54.958 --> 00:16:58.000
My next post will cover the menu
in depth, but for now,

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.667
my whole outlook on life has changed.

00:17:00.667 --> 00:17:02.833
They used all kinds of
self-sufficient ingredients,

00:17:02.833 --> 00:17:06.500
turning a poor location to their advantage.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.833
"Your faults and weaknesses can be weapons."

00:17:09.833 --> 00:17:13.417
Hearing my friend who works there say that,

00:17:13.417 --> 00:17:16.500
I thought about
how guilty I felt to be so spoiled,

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.458
hiding in the shadow of my big-shot father.

00:17:19.458 --> 00:17:22.958
I was such a dummy.

00:17:22.958 --> 00:17:23.667
"Yuji Norita" "Curious about a place? I'll fly right over!"

00:17:23.667 --> 00:17:27.292
"Yuji Norita" "Curious about a place? I'll fly right over!"
The allowance I'd been pampered with--that's <i>my </i>weapon.

00:17:27.292 --> 00:17:29.000
"Yuji Norita" "Curious about a place? I'll fly right over!"
And I want it to help people,

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:32.458
so I'll just make the most of it
and post my recommendations.

00:17:32.458 --> 00:17:36.792
First, the life-changing mountaintop café.

00:17:36.792 --> 00:17:37.875
--You've only got one day left to taste it!

00:17:37.875 --> 00:17:40.708
--Welcome!
--You've only got one day left to taste it!

00:17:40.708 --> 00:17:44.458
We all ran ourselves ragged after that.

00:17:44.458 --> 00:17:46.542
With every new order, we foraged,

00:17:46.542 --> 00:17:47.542
cooked,

00:17:47.542 --> 00:17:48.500
served,

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.167
and sold.

00:17:50.167 --> 00:17:52.917
Our friends and acquaintances

00:17:52.917 --> 00:17:53.750
kept coming,

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:54.625
and coming,

00:17:54.625 --> 00:17:56.375
and coming!

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:07.083
Uh-oh! We're about to
run out of acorn noodles!

00:18:07.083 --> 00:18:09.500
We sold more than we thought we would.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.542
But the A Class will have made more money.

00:18:12.542 --> 00:18:15.917
The "tastes of the mountain"
side menu is selling well, too.

00:18:15.917 --> 00:18:18.500
Let's stick it out with those
in the time we have left!

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.958
If we go a little further into the mountain,

00:18:20.958 --> 00:18:23.000
we can build up our reserves a bit.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.000
Hmm...

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.125
No--let's end it here.

00:18:28.125 --> 00:18:30.250
But then we can't win.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.500
That's all right.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:35.083
Any more foraging and we'll
destroy the mountain's ecosystem.

00:18:35.083 --> 00:18:36.417
Yeah...

00:18:36.417 --> 00:18:41.250
The actions of all creatures
contribute to our deeper interconnection.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:47.833
Did you sense all the connections
fate has blessed you with?

00:18:47.833 --> 00:18:50.708
Those who've taught you,
those you've helped,

00:18:50.708 --> 00:18:54.042
those you've caused trouble for,
those who've caused trouble for you.

00:18:54.042 --> 00:18:58.792
Those you've fought as rivals,
only to better one other.

00:18:58.792 --> 00:19:02.875
Aw! So today turned out to be
another lesson after all.

00:19:02.875 --> 00:19:06.167
Dammit. I really wanted to win, too.

00:19:10.208 --> 00:19:12.833
I'm sorry! We're all sold out--

00:19:12.833 --> 00:19:16.833
Oh, are you? You <i>were </i>very popular.

00:19:18.625 --> 00:19:20.917
Mom...

00:19:20.917 --> 00:19:24.833
Here you go: our last
crimson-glory-vine juice. It's tasty.

00:19:24.833 --> 00:19:26.250
Thanks.

00:19:27.333 --> 00:19:32.542
Your class is really something.
I see why you want to stay.

00:19:32.542 --> 00:19:33.958
Yeah.

00:19:35.083 --> 00:19:39.792
Nagisa, what happened
here the other night...

00:19:39.792 --> 00:19:43.667
Looking at your back, I knew:

00:19:43.667 --> 00:19:48.250
My son was separate from me.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:52.167
And graduating from me--that was no bluff.

00:19:52.167 --> 00:19:57.083
Somewhere along the way,
you'd found the strength to do just that.

00:20:00.125 --> 00:20:05.625
But, Nagisa... at least
stay with me till you come of age.

00:20:05.625 --> 00:20:11.042
Then you can do whatever you like.

00:20:11.042 --> 00:20:14.458
But I <i>did </i>get to be your mother, after all.

00:20:14.458 --> 00:20:18.125
Let me worry about you for a while longer.

00:20:18.125 --> 00:20:19.542
Okay!

00:20:20.708 --> 00:20:23.250
All of the connections
we encounter in this world

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:26.417
serve as teachers who nurture us.

00:20:26.417 --> 00:20:30.500
How about making today
the day you were born?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.917
The connections you gave me...

00:20:34.917 --> 00:20:38.250
Am I doing a good job passing them along?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.792
Hey.

00:20:39.792 --> 00:20:42.667
Nagisa's mother apologized.

00:20:42.667 --> 00:20:44.583
I understand she tried to set a fire?

00:20:44.583 --> 00:20:46.958
Yes. But that's water under the bridge.

00:20:46.958 --> 00:20:51.375
And she whispered something
to me as she left...

00:20:51.375 --> 00:20:55.708
Said she'd keep my <i>wig </i>a <i>secret</i>?!
What's the meaning of this?

00:20:59.167 --> 00:21:01.292
That A Class is amazing!

00:21:01.292 --> 00:21:03.542
They beat the high-schoolers
to come out on top!

00:21:03.542 --> 00:21:05.208
That's Asano for you.

00:21:05.208 --> 00:21:08.208
"School Festival: Overall Results"
But the E Class stands out, too.

00:21:08.208 --> 00:21:11.292
"School Festival: Overall Results"
Came in third even after shutting down halfway through day two!

00:21:11.292 --> 00:21:14.292
"School Festival: Overall Results"
How would it've turned out if they'd stayed till the end?

00:21:14.292 --> 00:21:15.583
Did you go?

00:21:15.583 --> 00:21:18.625
Well, it was on TV--I got all curious, y'know?

00:21:18.625 --> 00:21:22.250
Here I thought the E Class
was this hellish place.

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:24.625
Being all self-sufficient
out in nature like that?

00:21:24.625 --> 00:21:27.167
They might actually have it pretty good!

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:48.000
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:53.375
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.375 --> 00:21:59.042
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:59.042 --> 00:22:04.208
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.208 --> 00:22:15.583
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.583 --> 00:22:21.167
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:25.583
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.583 --> 00:22:32.417
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.417 --> 00:22:37.917
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.917 --> 00:22:43.417
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.417 --> 00:23:02.102
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
